llenging Russia's  assertions to having taken these  Ukrainian pieces of territory in water  and so that the Russian game here is  what the this area of Ukraine is of  Crimea it's ours well the first off that  is the first thing they say it is theirs  they're never giving it back they've  annexed if they say it's done but  secondly it's no matter what they do and  in this case they've actually fired on  Ukrainian naval vessels no firing back  by the Ukrainians by the way they've  then adopted the people they've  confiscated the ships and then they  blame the Ukrainians for doing that so  what's the United States gonna do about  it  well I think the first thing is we were  coordinating very closely with our  European allies and partners we have a  robust policy of sanctions in place we  work with Ukrainians on strengthening  their defense capabilities trying to  strengthen resiliency in Ukraine and our  European allies are doing the same  there's talk as we just saw on this  report about possible additional  sanctions from Europe we think that's  worth considering alternatively there  are sanctions on the books that perhaps  are not being implemented as rigorously  as they could be and that's something  else that some of our European allies  could okay you see the world looks on  and says well sanctions have already  been applied and Russia just keeps  marching around that area around Crimea  and say yeah despite the sanctions this  is ours this is ours and we'll have that  as well and I think I think that that  misses a couple of things first off I  think this could have been a lot worse  and I think the pressure that the West  has put back against Russia for having  invaded eastern Ukraine in particular  and applying sanctions there has created  some deterrent effect and Russia not  wanting to escalate in a full-scale  conflict not seeking to take new  territory I think that the defensive  support for Ukraine contributes to that  as well I also think that there's a lot  of discussion in Moscow now is this  really working out for Russia when you  saw what happened a few weeks ago with  Ukrainian Orthodox Church for example  they're demanding independence from the  russian orthodox church precisely  because the Ukrainian people are  alienated because of Russia's invasion  of Ukraine and killing Ukrainians so  that they've lost the goodwill of  Ukrainian people  have been there for centuries so it's a  it's a major loss for Russia really do  you see any role for a military response  in this I don't see any any desire by  anybody to fight against Russia to  retake this territory the Ukrainians  cannot and should not do that there's no  desire in the West to do that but what  we need to do is to deter further  Russian advances as being too costly and  too useless for them in order to create  the conditions for a negotiation to  re-establish peace and restore the  territory but do you think do you  realistically expect the the territory  to be reestablished you talk about  deterring Russia from further expansion  and my reading of the situation is that  once Russia has that bit of Ukraine  it'll it'll be happy that this is what  it wanted it's got it now no I don't  think that's right I think particularly  if you look at the DOM bus the part of  eastern Ukraine where there is still  active fighting every night this is not  territory that is terribly important to  Russia as the territory in itself it is  because it provides a foothold into the  rest of Ukraine provides a means of  influence the problem is that that  influence is backfired it has produced  exactly the opposite of what Russia  wanted so there is an incentive for  Russia to say let you know let's  negotiate a peace agreement here and  what the Minsk agreements actually say  is that the territory would be restored  to Ukrainian control and Russia is a  party to those agreements so it's a  matter of finding the mechanisms can we  get this implemented so that we can at  least establish peace in that part  Crimea it's gonna be a longer-term  problem but in eastern Ukraine I think  there is some hope good token do you  thank you for joining us i kurt volker  are you a special representative for  ukraine thank you
 

